      "headline": "When the Trusted Recipe Fails Every Time",
      "keyInsight": "Nobody invents a radical new method when everything runs smoothly. Think of an old family recipe you have baked for decades. One afternoon, the bread collapses into sticky grey dough. You blame the oven temperature. You blame bad yeast. You buy fresh flour and clean your baking pans. You try five more times, but the loaves keep failing. Only when sheer desperation sets in do you admit the original recipe was flawed. Fresh discoveries never arrive because someone casually wondered about a new path. They arrive because the old tools broke down completely. Brilliant breakthroughs demand genuine breakdown first.",
